<article class="env-lemma" id="043Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/043Z">Lemma <span data-tag="043Z">78.11.4</span>.</a> Let $B \to S$ as in Section <a href="/tag/043A" data-tag="043A">78.3</a>. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over $B$. In the commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ &  U &  \\  R \ar[d]_ s \ar[ru]^ t &  R \times _{s, U, t} R \ar[l]^-{\text{pr}_0} \ar[d]^{\text{pr}_1} \ar[r]_-c &  R \ar[d]^ s \ar[lu]_ t \\  U &  R \ar[l]_ t \ar[r]^ s &  U }  \]
</div>
  <p> the two lower squares are fibre product squares. Moreover, the triangle on top (which is really a square) is also cartesian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
